[brief] Warning: none of the available tools is a hydrodynamics or baryonic emulator. I had literature search tools only, so I did not compute any z=0 Pk-ratio values. Any number like that has to come from an
**Survey** — 34 tools on 3 servers, 6 read-only probes, 23 papers found.

Warning: none of the available tools is a hydrodynamics or baryonic emulator. I had literature search tools only, so I did not compute any z=0 Pk-ratio values. Any number like that has to come from an emulator the team installs (BACCO 2011.15018, BCemu 2108.08863, syren-baryon 2506.08783) or from published simulation tables. What the literature says: hydrodynamical simulations (OWLS/cosmo-OWLS/BAHAMAS 1105.1075 and 2309.06479, Horizon-AGN 1801.08559, IllustrisTNG/CAMELS 2511.10634 and 2301.02231, FLAMINGO 2410.17109) agree that baryons cause a small boost at k < 0.1 h/Mpc. Suppression then starts around k ~ 0.1-0.3 h/Mpc, reaches a minimum of roughly 10-30% at k ~ 5-20 h/Mpc depending on the model, and turns upward at higher k where stars and cooled gas concentrate matter. The physics: AGN feedback (thermal or kinetic/jet energy from black-hole accretion) pushes gas out of groups and clusters (about 10^13-10^14.5 Msun/h) past the virial radius. This lowers the halos' baryon fraction and makes their mass profiles shallower. The suppression therefore tracks halo gas fractions closely, which leads to empirical predictors based on cluster f_gas and f_star (2309.02920, 2509.04552, 2409.05716). For weak lensing: without modelling, feedback biases S8 low on small angular scales. Some papers argue that stronger-than-fiducial nonlinear suppression could partly explain the lensing-CMB S8 tension (2206.11794, 2305.09827, 2403.12967). DES Y3 small-scale analyses (2303.05537, 2206.08591), joint X-ray, tSZ and kSZ fits (2110.02228, 2109.04458) and recent kSZ+X-ray+GGL work (2512.02954) point to feedback that is relatively strong but still uncertain. For Stage IV surveys this is a leading systematic: the suppression needs percent-level modelling up to k ~ 10 h/Mpc or it must be marginalised over.

Quantities worth checking: Ratio S(k) = P_hydro/P_DMO at z=0 for k = 0.1-20 h/Mpc, at a fiducial feedback point and a strong-AGN point (for example, BACCO M_c = 10^14 vs 10^15 Msun/h, or FLAMINGO fiducial vs a fgas-8sigma-like model); Depth and position (k_min) of the suppression minimum, and the k where suppression reaches 1% and 5%; Upturn at high k caused by stellar cooling; Dependence of the suppression on Omega_b/Omega_m (the cosmic baryon fraction); Gas fraction in clusters (about 10^14 Msun) vs suppression at k ~ 1 h/Mpc; Bias on S8 if the suppression is ignored; requires cosmic-shear xi_+ or C_ell with and without S(k).
