**Finding:** I ran the HACC Pk-ratio emulator at z=0 with kappa_w=3, M_seed=1.3, omega_m=0.142 and sigma_8=0.81 held fixed. Strong-AGN point (e_w=1.0, v_kin=12000 km/s, eps_kin=12, all at their upper range edges): k(1%)=0.53 h/Mpc, k(5%)=1.86 h/Mpc, S(k=1)=0.975 +/- 0.002, S(k=3.7)=0.892 +/- 0.007. Weak-AGN point (e_w=0.2, v_kin=1000 km/s, eps_kin=0.2, all at their lower edges): no suppression. Instead S rises above 1 to a peak of about 1.011 +/- 0.007 near k~2.4 h/Mpc, with S(k=1)=1.003 +/- 0.003 and S(k=3.7)=1.004 +/- 0.011. Compared with the fiducial (S(1)=0.979, k(1%)=0.59, k(5%)=2.11; finding f-023), the strong point adds only about 0.4% more suppression at k=1. Almost all of the AGN sensitivity lies between the weak and fiducial points.
