**Completed — Close the remaining literature gaps for the weak-lensing assessment and the citations. Add cite() entries for the key papers that do not yet have them (2410.17109, 2206.11794, 2305.09827, 2309.07959, 2605.04176, 2309.06479). Obtain the verbatim FLAMINGO 2309.07959 conclusion. Find any quoted fractional C_ell change or S8 bias in sigma from ignoring baryons, for example in 1105.1075, 2303.05537 or 2206.08591..** Partly done: 2 of the 3 success criteria are met (the FLAMINGO statement, and an explicit note that no C_ell or sigma-bias number was found); the citation criterion is short by one, with 4 of the required 5 papers cited. (1) Verbatim FLAMINGO 2309.07959 conclusion, read from its abstract (tc-...-27) and cited (tc-...-48): 'it is unlikely that baryon physics is driving this modification'. The abstract also states that baryonic effects are not large enough to remove the S8 tension, but that sentence could not be used as a validated quote because the spaces were lost in text extraction. (2) Validated cite() entries in /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-baryonic-pk/runs/261023_110038/references.bib cover 4 papers: 2309.07959, 2410.17109 ('lower gas fractions in groups and clusters lead to a stronger response'), 2309.06479 ('group-sized haloes') and 2605.04176 ('weaker than in other state-of-the-art simulations'). (3) The cite() calls for 2206.11794 and 2305.09827 failed quote validation, so these two papers are not yet in the bib (dead end x-05). Their abstract texts were read: Amon and Efstathiou argue that a stronger nonlinear suppression than assumed would reconcile KiDS-1000 with Planck; Preston et al. find that the DES Y3 suppression needed is still more extreme than recent simulations predict and must extend to k ~ 0.2 h/Mpc. (4) Finding f-022 collects these verbatim weak-lensing statements, plus two from abstracts: FLAMINGO 2410.17109 says its strongest-feedback response is in strong tension with X-ray gas fractions, and Astrid 2605.04176 finds no significant suppression at z=0. Finding f-025 records the bib status. (5) Not established: no fractional C_ell change at ell 500-5000 and no S8 bias in sigma from ignoring baryons was extracted, because the budget ran out before 1105.1075, 2303.05537 and 2206.08591 could be read. A_mod values were not re-read either. Open question q-10 asks a later wave to finish these with short ASCII-only quotes.
