[usage]
[critique] wave 1 wave: continue
**Critic, wave 1** — continue: 2 findings stand up to the evidence, 3 questioned ('Verbatim weak-lensing literature statements: FLAMINGO (2309.07959) concludes "some mechani': All six evidence excerpts (tc-...-27, -28, -29, -42, -43, -44) stop at the title, authors and affiliations, before any abstract text. None contains the quoted sentences. The validated FLAMINGO cite() call (tc-...-48) is not listed as evidence for this finding. The Preston+ wording is close to the quote that failed validation in tc-...-41, which means the claimed verbatim text was never confirmed against the source.; 'The HACC CRK-HACC Pk-ratio emulator, evaluated at z=0 for the mid-design fiducial point (k': The only data excerpt (tc-...-46) ends at k=0.117 h/Mpc. None of the headline numbers can be checked against it: k(1%)=0.59, k(5%)=2.11, S(1)=0.979+/-0.001 and S(3.7)=0.901+/-0.004. The part that can be checked is slightly misstated: at k=0.0859, S=0.99986, a deviation of 1.4e-4, not 'within 1e-4 at k<0.09'. The parameter units do convert correctly: v_kin 0.65 x1e4 km/s and eps_kin 0.61 x10.; 'I ran the HACC Pk-ratio emulator at z=0 with kappa_w=3, M_seed=1.3, omega_m=0.142 and sigm': The CSV excerpts (tc-...-61, -62) also end at k=0.117 h/Mpc, so these values cannot be verified from the quoted evidence: S(1)=0.975 and 1.003, k(1%) and k(5%) for the strong point, and the weak-point peak of 1.011 at k~2.4. Both points sit on the edges of the design ranges, which critique c-05 warned risks GP extrapolation. A weak-point S>1 of about 1% at k~2.4 is not physically implausible for weak-feedback runs, but it needs an off-edge robustness check before it is reported as physical. The claimed 0.4% strong-vs-fiducial difference at k=1 is about 1.8 combined sigma (0.004 vs sqrt(0.001^2+0.002^2)=0.0022), so it is only marginally significant.).

Issues: The core quantitative deliverables (S_min, k_min, S(k=5), k_max) are still unmeasured. The measured values are not backed by quoted CSV rows, because both file readers truncated at k~3.7 h/Mpc and the evidence excerpts stop at k~0.12.; The summary states that no curve shows a boost at k<0.1. The weak-point CSV shows S=1.00014 at k=0.086, a small boost in exactly the sense the brief describes. It is negligible, but the statement as written does not match the data.; The literature benchmarks in the summary are not traced to any cite() quote or finding: OWLS S(1)~0.90, the 'BCemu and FLAMINGO-like minima', and the weak point resembling Astrid. Critique c-05 raised this in wave 0 and it is still unaddressed..
