**Next steps after wave 1** — With one wave and about 17 tool calls left, the priority is to turn the existing emulator runs into verifiable numbers and to source the weak-lensing assessment. d-08 is reopened because its only blocker was the tool-call budget. Its outputs exist but were never read. To answer the critic's cosmology-mismatch issue, it should build the f_gas-vs-S(1) relation and the z=0 versus z=1 trend from the d-08 Pk-ratio and fGas files at its own cosmology (omega_m=0.1375, sigma_8=0.80), and rerun the weak point into its own subdirectory. The Omega_b/Omega_m part of d-08 is settled as not supported (f-024), and the sigma_8 and omega_m variation is optional if calls remain. A new child of d-07 closes the k-range gaps (S_min, k_min, k_max) with quoted rows and runs the robustness check inside the design bounds that c-05 and c-06 requested. The one-at-a-time AGN-channel scan suggested by the critic is dropped for budget reasons. A new child of d-09 cites the two key S8-tension papers with ASCII-only quotes and extracts sourced S8-bias numbers and FLAMINGO bracket values. The toy Limber projection is not planned because no code-execution tool is available. No facility run is needed, since the task does not request HPC dispatch and the emulator runs on a hosted server.

New lines of investigation: Close the d-07 measurement gaps. Read the full d07 Pk-ratio CSVs past k~3.7 h/Mpc to get S(k=5), S_min, k_min and the emulator k_max, backing each value with quoted CSV rows. Then test whether the weak-point boost and the strong-point saturation survive moving the parameters just inside the design bounds.; Make the weak-lensing assessment quantitative and sourced. Cite 2206.11794 and 2305.09827 using short ASCII-only quotes, extract at least one quoted S8 or C_ell bias number from ignoring baryons, and extract FLAMINGO fiducial and strong-feedback S(k) values from 2410.17109 to bracket the HACC points..
