[tool] d-11 post_finding {"claim": "Sourced weak-lensing numbers (from the paper text, not computed): KiDS-1000 cosmic-shear S8 = 0.759 (+0.024/-0.021) is about 9% below Planck TTTEEE+P
[finding] f-030 Sourced weak-lensing numbers (from the paper text, not computed): KiDS-1000 cosmic-shear S8 = 0.759 (+0.024/-0.021) is about 9% below Planck TTTEEE+Plens S8 = 0
**Finding:** Sourced weak-lensing numbers (from the paper text, not computed): KiDS-1000 cosmic-shear S8 = 0.759 (+0.024/-0.021) is about 9% below Planck TTTEEE+Plens S8 = 0.829 +/- 0.012, a ~2.4-2.7 sigma discrepancy (2206.11794). DES Y3 cosmic shear gives S8 = 0.772 (+0.018/-0.017). Planck LCDM fits KiDS shear if the nonlinear power is modulated by A_mod ~ 0.69 (2305.09827 eq. 1), and for DES Y3 the suppression needed must extend to k ~ 0.2 h/Mpc. This is a bound on how large a small-scale suppression could shift S8; it is not a direct S8 bias from ignoring baryons.
[tool] tc-261023_1-w2-d-11-98 -> ok: Recorded finding f-030.
[tool] d-11 post_finding {"claim": "FLAMINGO 2410.17109 text (Sec. 4.4.1, Fig. 11): the fgas-8sigma thermal and jet models closely resemble cosmo-OWLS AGN with Delta T_AGN = 8.3 and 8.5
[finding] f-031 FLAMINGO 2410.17109 text (Sec. 4.4.1, Fig. 11): the fgas-8sigma thermal and jet models closely resemble cosmo-OWLS AGN with Delta T_AGN = 8.3 and 8.5. Only Illu
**Finding:** FLAMINGO 2410.17109 text (Sec. 4.4.1, Fig. 11): the fgas-8sigma thermal and jet models closely resemble cosmo-OWLS AGN with Delta T_AGN = 8.3 and 8.5. Only Illustris and cosmo-OWLS-AGN-8.7 lie beyond the emulator's reach. The emulator is accurate to better than 1% up to k = 10 h/Mpc and z = 3, and the cosmology dependence is about 1% at k < 10 h/Mpc. The extracted text gives no numerical S(k) values for the fiducial or strong models (they appear only in Fig. 11, whose y-axis spans 0.65-1.10), so the HACC fiducial S(1)=0.979 and strong S(1)=0.975 points cannot be placed numerically against FLAMINGO using cited values.
