**Finding:** HACC emulator at z=0 (kappa_w=3, M_seed=1.3, omega_m=0.1375, sigma_8=0.8). The gas fraction within R500c at M500c=7.94e13 Msun/h (1.26e14 Msun/h in brackets) is: weak (e_w=0.2, v_kin=0.1, eps_kin=0.02) 0.1396+/-0.0024 (0.1438); fiducial (e_w=0.6, v_kin=0.65, eps_kin=0.61) 0.1099+/-0.0011 (0.1229); strong (e_w=1.0, v_kin=1.2, eps_kin=1.2) 0.1111+/-0.0020 (0.1237). At the same points, S(k=1.013 h/Mpc) = 1.0022+/-0.0025 (weak), 0.9766+/-0.0010 (fiducial) and 0.9733+/-0.0018 (strong). Lower f_gas goes with stronger suppression: a 0.03 drop in f_gas moves 1-S(1) from about -0.002 to about 0.024. The fiducial and strong points do not differ significantly in f_gas (difference 0.001, within 1 sigma), even though the strong point suppresses about 0.3% more.
