[tool] d-08 post_finding {"claim": "HACC Pk-ratio redshift evolution, same cosmology (omega_m=0.1375, sigma_8=0.8). Fiducial point: S(k=1.013) is 0.9766 at z=0 and 0.9848+/-0.0010 at z=
[finding] f-033 HACC Pk-ratio redshift evolution, same cosmology (omega_m=0.1375, sigma_8=0.8). Fiducial point: S(k=1.013) is 0.9766 at z=0 and 0.9848+/-0.0010 at z=1; S(k=3.71
**Finding:** HACC Pk-ratio redshift evolution, same cosmology (omega_m=0.1375, sigma_8=0.8). Fiducial point: S(k=1.013) is 0.9766 at z=0 and 0.9848+/-0.0010 at z=1; S(k=3.71) is 0.8924 at z=0 and 0.9458 at z=1; k(1%) moves from about 0.55 h/Mpc (z=0) to about 0.78 h/Mpc (z=1), and k(5%) from about 1.92 to about 3.09 h/Mpc. Strong point: S(1.013) is 0.9733 at z=0 and 0.9881+/-0.0016 at z=1; S(3.71) is 0.8852 at z=0 and 0.9620+/-0.0057 at z=1; k(1%) moves from about 0.51 to about 0.90 h/Mpc. k(5%) is about 1.74 h/Mpc at z=0, and S never reaches 0.95 for k<3.73 at z=1, where the curve flattens near 0.962 over k=3.4-3.7 h/Mpc. Suppression is therefore weaker at z=1 and starts at higher k. At z=1 the strong point suppresses less than the fiducial, so the ordering seen at z=0 reverses.
