**Completed — Make the weak-lensing assessment quantitative and sourced. Cite 2206.11794 and 2305.09827 using short ASCII-only quotes, extract at least one quoted S8 or C_ell bias number from ignoring baryons, and extract FLAMINGO fiducial and strong-feedback S(k) values from 2410.17109 to bracket the HACC points..** Partly done: two of the three success criteria are met. The third, placing the HACC points against FLAMINGO with cited numbers, is not met. (1) Done: 2206.11794 and 2305.09827 are now in /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-research-baryonic-pk/runs/261023_110038/references.bib under the keys arxiv220611794 and arxiv230509827. Their short ASCII quotes passed validation: 'suppressed more strongly on non-linear scales than', 'about 9% lower than the Planck value', 'is still more extreme than predictions from recent numerical simulations' and 'is not as strong as inferred using KiDS data' (finding f-029). (2) Done, with a caveat: I have sourced S8 numbers, but they are not a direct 'bias from ignoring baryons' number. KiDS-1000 cosmic shear gives S8 = 0.759 (+0.024/-0.021), about 9% below Planck TTTEEE+Plens S8 = 0.829 +/- 0.012, a discrepancy of about 2.4-2.7 sigma. DES Y3 cosmic shear gives S8 = 0.772 (+0.018/-0.017). Planck LCDM fits the KiDS shear data if the non-linear power is scaled by A_mod ~ 0.69, and for DES Y3 the suppression has to extend to k ~ 0.2 h/Mpc. Only the '9% lower' phrase is cite()-validated; the other numbers were read from the extracted text (finding f-030). (3) Not met: the FLAMINGO 2410.17109 text gives no numerical S(k) values for its fiducial or strongest-feedback models. Those curves appear only in Fig. 11 (z=0, y-axis 0.65-1.10). What the text does state: the fgas-8sigma thermal and jet models closely resemble cosmo-OWLS Delta T_AGN = 8.3 and 8.5, the emulator is accurate to better than 1% up to k = 10 h/Mpc, the cosmology dependence is about 1%, and only Illustris and cosmo-OWLS 8.7 lie beyond its reach (finding f-031). So the HACC fiducial S(1)=0.979 and strong S(1)=0.975 (f-023, f-026) cannot be bracketed against FLAMINGO using cited values only. (4) Effect on d-07: its comparisons with FLAMINGO and BCemu minima, and with 'OWLS AGN S(1)~0.90', are still unsourced and should be dropped or marked qualitative. The strong-suppression S8 argument (Amon and Efstathiou; Preston et al.) is now sourced. Not attempted: reading 2303.05537 and 2206.08591. Still open (q-13): extract Fig. 11 of 2410.17109 with get_paper_figures to get numerical S(k) values, and quote an S8 shift from the small-scale DES Y3 analyses.
