**Critic, wave 2** — continue: 2 findings stand up to the evidence, 5 questioned ('The d07 fiducial HACC Pk-ratio CSV (z=0) extends far beyond k~3.7 h/Mpc. Its rows are k,y_': The quoted excerpt of tc-...-85 shows rows only from k=7.4515 to about 7.61. The rows claimed at k=9.006, 10.01 and 11.27 do not appear in any quoted excerpt. The claim also calls the decrease 'monotonic', but the d-10 summary itself reports small local upticks. The conclusion that there is no minimum up to k~11 h/Mpc is plausible, but it needs the actual tail rows quoted, including the true last row for k_max.; 'Sourced weak-lensing numbers (from the paper text, not computed): KiDS-1000 cosmic-shear S': Both evidence excerpts (tc-...-82 and tc-...-83) end inside the abstracts. None of the claimed numbers (S8=0.759, 0.829+/-0.012, 0.772, the 2.4-2.7 sigma tension, A_mod~0.69, 'eq. 1') appears in them. Only the '9% lower' phrase is cite()-validated, and that sits in f-029. Attributing A_mod~0.69 to 2305.09827 eq. 1 also needs checking: the value originates in Amon and Efstathiou 2206.11794 for KiDS.; 'FLAMINGO 2410.17109 text (Sec. 4.4.1, Fig. 11): the fgas-8sigma thermal and jet models clo': The excerpts show only the FLAMINGO header and a Fig. 10 caption about the LS8 cosmology. The stated content is not in the quoted evidence: fgas-8sigma resembling cosmo-OWLS 8.3/8.5, accuracy better than 1% to k=10 and z=3, about 1% cosmology dependence, and only Illustris and cosmo-OWLS 8.7 being out of reach. The negative claim that the text contains no numbers is also unverified.; 'HACC emulator at z=0 (kappa_w=3, M_seed=1.3, omega_m=0.1375, sigma_8=0.8). The gas fractio': The f_gas values are confirmed by the CSV excerpts (0.10992/0.12286 fiducial, 0.11113/0.12374 strong, 0.13955/0.14379 weak). However, the Pk-ratio excerpts (tc-86, 87, 89) stop at k~0.117. The S(k=1.013) values 1.0022, 0.9766 and 0.9733 are not visible, so the suppression half of the f_gas-S relation is unsupported by the quoted evidence.).

Issues: The strong point has a higher f_gas than the fiducial at all three mass bins (for example 0.0985 vs 0.0956 at 5e13). This non-monotonic behaviour as feedback parameters increase suggests the strong corner sits at a design edge or is GP-extrapolated. It should be interpreted together with the pending inside-bound test rather than read as physics.; d-08 used omega_m=0.1375 and sigma_8=0.8, while d-07 and d-10 used 0.142 and 0.81. Fiducial S(3.7) is 0.901 vs 0.892 and k(1%) is 0.59 vs 0.55 across the two sets. Any combined table must keep the cosmologies separate, and this difference is itself an informal estimate of cosmology dependence.; The task asks for the impact of baryons on weak lensing. No quantitative propagation of the HACC S(k) into a shear C_ell or an S8 shift has been made, and no sourced S8-bias number from ignoring baryons has been extracted. This is the largest remaining gap in the deliverable..
